ls and Agent`) content\ninto Foundry `notes/`; add a `map.json` entry naming it. Extend the suite: `notes/`\nis populated and the drift check stays GREEN. Accept: `pytest -v` GREEN.\nFINALIZE (manual, cross-repo): repoint ~8 external refs (incl. aurora README/CLAUDE/NOTES);\nafter drift-GREEN, delete the loose source.\n\n## Wave 2 â€” Stage .critique-scratch (+ v1.1) into the Foundry (copy-only)\nDeliver: copy both into Foundry `tools/critique-scratch/`; add a `map.json` entry;\nmark **copy-only** (a live write target of `t2r-proxy.mjs` â€” source stays). Extend\nthe suite: copies present and match a recorded content hash; drift GREEN.\nAccept: `pytest -v` GREEN. (No source deletion â€” copy-only by design.)\n\n## Wave 3 â€” Reconcile Expert-Coder-Win11 reference\nDeliver: record the canonical source (`skills-master/expert-coder`) in `map.json`;\nstage only genuinely Foundry-authored notes. Extend the suite: the MAP names the\ncanonical and no Foundry copy claims authorship over it. Accept: `pytest -v` GREEN.\nFINALIZE (manual): triage the ~13 \"canonical\" refs; reconcile/delete the loose\n`C:\\dev\\Expert-Coder-Win11`.\n\n## Wave 4 â€” Governance docs\nDeliver: Foundry `docs/` with `SKILL-PRODUCTIONIZATION-CHECKLIST.md` (copied from\nAgentic-Home), a seeded `CONTRIBUTING.md`, the staged `SKILL.template.md` (from\n`C:\\dev\\Skill-Foundry-SKILL.template.md`), and a `map.json` pointer to the\n`researchOne` gold-standard exemplar. Extend the suite: each governance file present\nand non-empty; the template parses; the checklist contains its 5 gates.\nAccept: `pytest -v` GREEN.\n\n## Wave 5 â€” Lock in the project-manager invariant\nDeliver TWO things so the wave has a real in-repo deliverable (a pure test-only wave\ntrips the vacuous-GREEN guard): (a) add a `project-manager` entry to `map.json` â€”\n`\"canonical_external\": true`, `\"source\": \"C:\\\\dev\\\\Agentic-Home\\\\skills-master\\\\project-manager\"`,\n`\"targets\": []`, with a `note` that skills-master is the